s unacceptable state brutality,\\\" said Phelim Kine, deputy Asia director at Human Rights Watch, in a statement Saturday. \\\"President Widodo should recognize that the death penalty is not a crime deterrent but an unjustifiable and barbaric punishment. Widodo should promote Indonesia as a rights-respecting democracy by joining the countries that have abolished capital punishment.\\\"\\n\",\"answer\":\"Nine out of ten prisoners on death row in Indonesia have been given 72 hours notice of their execution. The French prisoner, Serge Atlaoui, has had his execution delayed due to a challenge filed with the State Administrative Court. Mary Jane Veloso, a Filipino maid, has been told that her execution will take place on Tuesday, April 28. Veloso claims that she unknowingly carried drugs into Indonesia and was set up by a drug syndicate. The Australian prisoners, Andrew Chan and Myuran Sukumaran, part of the \\\"Bali Nine\\\" smuggling ring, have been notified that their execution will be carried out \\\"imminently.\\\" The Australian government has appealed to Indonesian President Joko Widodo to reconsider his refusal to grant clemency. The Secretary-General of the United Nations, Ban Ki-moon, has also called on Indonesia to reverse their decision to execute the prisoners. Human Rights Watch has urged President Widodo to spare the lives of the prisoners and end capital punishment in Indonesia.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":184},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":184,\"byte_end\":268},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":268,\"byte_end\":286},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":286,\"byte_end\":409},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":409,\"byte_end\":631},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":631,\"byte_end\":795},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":795,\"byte_end\":948},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":948,\"byte_end\":1079},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":1079,\"byte_end\":1295},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":1295,\"byte_end\":1326},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":1326,\"byte_end\":1382},{\"index